# NOTE
# can create incrementally, one type of child window at a time, e.g.,
#   - Table/View window
#       Table name label [Order By v] # No Order By if view has ORDER BY?
#       Field name labels
#       Rows of data
#   - SELECT window for entering queries using text editor with
#       SQL color syntax highlighting
#   - Structure window for the db structure (tables, views, indexes,
#       triggers, etc.)
#   - Pragma window
#   - Record window
#       Table name label |< < > >| [Order By v]
#       Fieldname Fieldvalue
#       -except if field type is BLOB-
#   	if jpg|png|svg show
#   	    Fieldname:
#   	    Label with image
#   	if ste|tkt|tktz show
#   	    Fieldname:
#   	    ste with text
#   	else
#   	    Fieldname “BLOB (n,nnn bytes)”
#
# NOTE
# Whenever a new database is opened look for databasename.sqn or failing
# that glob *.sqn & if there is exactly one use that for metadata;
# If the user sets metadata, i.e., says this field is jpg or bool etc.,
# then save databasename.sqn when the database (or Sequin) is closed.
#   .sqn file is ini-style e.g.,
#     [table name]
#     field name: field_interpretation
#   where field_interpretation is one of:
#   bool png jpg svg tkt tktz ste blob (default)

